Failure-path test: NOT_TESTABLE. The proposed repro (revoke Accessibility permission mid-flight) does not affect writeObjects: — NSPasteboard operations run through the pasteboard server (pbs) and are independent of TCC Accessibility permissions. Revoking Accessibility would only fail AXUIElementPostKeyboardEvent, not the NSPasteboard write. Forcing writeObjects to return false requires either (a) lazy/promise-based clipboard content (e.g., Finder file copy), which requires Finder interaction prohibited by guardrails, or (b) a pasteboard server fault, which cannot be engineered from outside the process. No guardrail-safe method exists to trigger the writeObjects failure path.
